            "forgeweave:traits": [],
            "minecraft:damage": 0,
            "minecraft:max_damage": 250
        },
        count: 1,
        id: "forgeweave:pickaxe"
    },
    what: "#969: the gem stacks are minecraft:diamond rather than apotheosis:gem because no unit-test item registry holds an Apotheosis item, and what this fixture pins is the shape, not the gem. An all-iron pickaxe carrying three sockets (the socketed modifier at level 3, which is its cap) with gems in the first and third and the second left empty -- forgeweave:sockets is vanilla's ItemContainerContents, so empty sockets are dropped from the encoded form and each gem carries its own slot index, which is what makes a gem in socket three decode back into socket three. The sockets themselves are the modifier's level, not part of this component, so a stack with no socketed entry has no sockets whatever the component says."
}
